<%
  account_link = if authenticated?
    link_to("hosted account", dashboard_path, class: "ui-btn-link")
  else
    link_to("hosted account", sign_up_path, class: "ui-btn-link")
  end
%>

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
  <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground/90 mb-2">
    Unlimited trial during open beta
  </h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8">
    How hosted accounts work while ugo is in early access.
  </p>

  <div class="space-y-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
    <p>
      ugo is in open beta. We hope to learn a lot from early users. During this period we want you to explore hosted ugo without worrying about a trial countdown.
    </p>

    <p>
      Every new <%= account_link %> starts on a free Basic trial with no credit card required. During open beta your trial does not end on a fixed schedule: if you keep using ugo, we automatically renew your trial so active workspaces stay open.
    <p>
    </p>
      Subscribe anytime through our <%= link_to "hosted plans", pricing_path, class: "ui-btn-link" %> if you want paid tier limits, or keep exploring while we are still in beta.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-2">How links and campaign tracking work</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        It's a link shortner, but also much more. ugo turns long URLs into short links you can share like <%= render "shared/url_badge", url: "ugo.cr/xxxxx" %>. Add UTM parameters with the built in URL builder and those tags ride along when someone clicks through to your site. 
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">  
        Your analytics platform reads them on the landing page the same way it always has, whether you use Google Analytics, Plausible, Fathom, or something else. ugo tracks clicks too, but campaign attribution stays with the tools you already trust.
      </p>

      <%= render "ui/card" do %>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground text-center mb-5">From short link to site analytics</p>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <% [
            { icon: "figure",   title: "Build in ugo",       body: "Paste your destination URL and add UTM tags with the URL builder." },
            { icon: "link",     title: "Share a short link", body: "Publish a short link on social, email, or ad campaigns." },
            { icon: "share_nodes", title: "Audience clicks", body: "Visitors hit your short link from any channel or device." },
            { icon: "arrow_path",  title: "ugo redirects",  body: "They land on your site with UTM parameters intact on the URL." },
            { icon: "chart_bar",   title: "Analytics reads UTMs", body: "Google Analytics, Plausible, Fathom, or your platform attributes the visit." }
          ].each_with_index do |step, index| %>
            <% if index > 0 %>
              <div class="flex justify-center text-muted-foreground/60">
                <%= render "shared/svg/chevron_down", class: "w-4 h-4" %>
              </div>
            <% end %>

            <div class="w-full rounded-md border border-border bg-page p-4 flex items-start gap-3">
                <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-primary-100 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-primary-600">
                  <%= render "shared/svg/#{step[:icon]}", class: "w-4 h-4" %>
                </div>
                <div class="min-w-0">
                  <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground"><%= step[:title] %></p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-0.5 leading-relaxed"><%= step[:body] %></p>
                </div>
              </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </section>

    <p>
      <%= link_to "Hosted plans", pricing_path, class: "ui-btn-link" %> run on ugo.cr with zero configuration. Create an account and you can shorten links, tag campaigns, preview social cards, and review click analytics from day one.
    </p>
    <p>
      Basic and Growth plans scale with your traffic. Dedicated plan adds your own subdomain and deep linking, along with unlimited use of a server's resources (no event tracking limit). You can also run a <%= link_to "self-hosted", self_host_path, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer", class: "ui-btn-link" %> instance on your own infrastructure if you want full control.
    </p>

    <p>
      The moment the open beta period is over standard trial length will apply and we will give plenty of notice before anything changes. Until then, try ugo, tell us what works, and help shape what comes next.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%= render "shared/footer" %>
</div>
